{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "983d9021-a163-44bb-ac1e-761e869bb0a6",
    "name": "PAIGS WildID -- Stage 0 (Import)",
    "description": "Manual test collection for the PAIGS WildID backend, Stage 0 (Import) only.\n\nUpdated 2026-09-23 for the CLAUDE.md rewrite: upload now goes into two independently-optional labeled slots, forward_read and reverse_read -- a single file is a first-class path, not a fallback.\n\nSetup:\n1. From backend/, run: uvicorn app.main:app --reload\n2. Import the PAIGS environment (postman/PAIGS.postman_environment.json) alongside this collection and select it.\n3. Run 'Happy path' top to bottom first -- it captures run_id into the environment for later requests. 'Errors' can be run independently, except 'Patch run - rejects empty label', which reuses run_id.\n\nTest data lives in postman/test-data/ (copies of backend/tests/fixtures/*.ab1, plus a plain-text file for exercising the extension-rejection case).\n\nThis collection will grow as later pipeline stages (format_check, ab1_extraction, sanity_check, ...) are built.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Happy path",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sanity check that the API is up before running anything else."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create run - forward + reverse reads",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/runs",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "runs"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Stage 0 (Import), two-read path. Uploads into the forward_read and reverse_read slots. Both single- and two-file are first-class per the current CLAUDE.md -- this is the two-file case. Saves run_id into the environment for the requests below.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "forward_read",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "/Users/mac/projects/paigs-wildid/postman/test-data/3100.ab1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "reverse_read",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "/Users/mac/projects/paigs-wildid/postman/test-data/3730.ab1"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('has id', () => pm.expect(body.id).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.test('current_stage is import', () => pm.expect(body.current_stage).to.eql('import'));",
                  "pm.test('status is in_progress', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('in_progress'));",
                  "pm.test('both filenames present, in slot order', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.original_filenames).to.eql(['3100.ab1', '3730.ab1']);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.environment.set('run_id', body.id);",
                  "pm.environment.set('run_sample_id', body.sample_id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create run - forward read only (single-file path)",
          "request": {
